- **Measured before READY, by the Linux SHAPE (the instrument: `TMPDIR=/tmp` in the real environment plus `RUNNER_TEMP` a persistent dot-free folder; the shape that read B2099's two hosted reds):** (a) both files in the lane, in the Linux shape and the own shape (`lane2127.sh`); (b) the eleven neighbour suites in the Linux shape (the lane's last run); (c) the WHOLE suite in the Linux shape once (step 5, `linux-update`, the run that also writes the counts); (d) the plain verify in the own shape at K (the CI predicate with the committed counts). The own shape keeps the wrapper shell's `TMPDIR` (printed, `/var/folders/...` here); **never unset `TMPDIR` to make an "own environment" control** (on this machine `os.tmpdir()` answers `/tmp` when it is unset: that is a Linux shape).
