## THE PROPERTY
**The property:** (A) both audit entries of the SCIM router (`scim_rate_limited` from the limiter, `scim_auth_failed` from the token check) record `path` as the pathname of the request as sent (the full mounted path, no query string, no fragment, no host, percent-encoding as sent, a trailing slash as sent), the `method`, and the `ip`, and exactly those three keys; they carry no token material and nothing that says why a token failed; a correct token writes neither entry; the other SCIM entries (a created user writes `scim_user_created` with its `userName` only) still write, unchanged; a cell goes red when either entry reads `req.path` again, reads `req.originalUrl`, loses `method`, or gains token material. (B) the CSP intake answers `null` for a `data:` address whose kept text holds a literal `@` (any case of the scheme, edge spaces, the BOM, a tab inside the scheme), in each of the three address fields of a report, in both report shapes (an object and the Reporting API array); a report with a directive is kept with a null address, and a report with no other field is dropped (the route answers its own 400); every other `data:` address, `data` alone, a `%40` inside a data: payload, and every other scheme are as before; the two landed shapes keep their own lines; a cell goes red when the refusal is removed, widened to all `data:` addresses or to all schemes, narrowed to one case, made to read the raw text, or made to read `%40` too. (C) nothing is built for the other SCIM entries, for `%40` in a data: payload, for a blob whose inner address is a data: address, or for any other RD-759 shape. **Tested shapes:** the lane's runs (red-first at BASE in both shapes, green in both, each mutation red on exactly its cells), the whole suite once in the Linux shape, the plain verify. **Shapes outside, said so:** the production setting's real boot (H1 runs the project's enforced shape, not a production deployment); a hosted instance; a reader of these entries outside the repository; the real route driven with a data: report over HTTP (the CSP cells call the module the route calls, once: S2 counts the call; the route's own 400 for an emptied report is pinned by the earlier route cells and by D4's `[]`); real Linux.

